{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1461826-princess-the-hopeful-\u2014-dream-or-vocation","id":1461826,"title":"Princess: the Hopeful \u2014 Dream or Vocation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-28T08:29:18-07:00","id":1461826,"title":"Princess: the Hopeful \u2014 Dream or Vocation?","content":"So, I've been attempting to read through both versions of Princess: the Hopeful, to get a sense of how they compare and contrast. It's not easy: they seem to be extremely similar in what they cover overall, with the single biggest difference appearing to be how each PDF is organized. Even their titular differences don't really seem to be all that different overall: each supplements Aspirations with a Princess-specific Aspiration variant that provides Luminous Beats as well as regular beats, and which need to be selfless rather than selfish in essence. <br /> <br /> Could I get someone who's more familiar with Princess to help out with identifying how the two versions of the game differ? As things stand, I'm looking at taking the Vocation manuscript as a baseline, and replacing the \u201cthree Aspirations + one Vocation\u201d bit with the \u201cthree Aspirations or Dreams + two Dreams\u201d bit from the Dream version; I like the concept of Dreams more than I like the concept of Vocations, but so far I'm finding the Vocational version of the game to be better organized and easier to understand. Is there anything else that the Dream version has to offer that the Vocation version doesn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T14:17:20-07:00","id":1461865,"title":"","content":"As best I can recall, the most important differences in the systems are in the Belief and Sensitivity rules. Echoes also work differently, and many Practical Magics in Dream are Charms in Vocation. I don't think there's anything actually <i>missing</i> in Vocation that's in Dream; it's mostly a matter of slightly different takes on the same material.<br /> <br /> Kings Raven has been spending his time writing a 2e version of Genius the Transgression lately, so Dream isn't getting updated nearly as much as Vocation is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T15:50:12-07:00","id":1461882,"title":"","content":"Vocation has more specialized charms as well as equilivents to the excellencys in Exalted<br /> <br /> Dreams offers a more bitter sweet ending to a princess who almost becomes a dethroned.<br /> <br /> Vocation makes it more diffricult to recover a stolen phlactery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}